This product includes logic ported from the security-guidance plugin in
https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official (plugins/security-guidance),
Copyright Anthropic, PBC, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). Ported parts, rewritten in JavaScript:

- the git-baseline diff: `git stash create` (or HEAD) at UserPromptSubmit, diff against
  it at Stop, untracked-file snapshot, "dirty now and changed since baseline" review set
  (lib/git.js, lib/changes.js, lib/hooks.js)
- the locked read-then-clear of per-session state at Stop, and restoring the consumed
  paths after a transient failure (lib/state.js, lib/runner.js)
- the rewake fire cap, the one-hour finding dedupe, the stop_hook_active loop guard, and
  the rewake framing and stdout rewakeSummary protocol (lib/runner.js, lib/claude.js,
  hooks/hooks.json)
- kill switches and a local log that never holds file contents (lib/config.js, lib/log.js)

The secret-redaction rules in lib/redact.js are adapted from gitleaks' default
